A||N||6||GT-maniac||Running with the EGR light on||||1||
Z||000000||GT-maniac||11-17-2000||01:45 PM||||Hi all, I have the usual fiero EGR problem with the EGR light coming on at highway speeds. I have a new EGR valve in but it didn't make any difference. Anyway my question is since I can't seem to fix the problem will it harm my engine to run long periods with the EGR malfunctioning like this ? I'm considering a 600 mile trip in the near future.||||reg||1
Z||000001||DaveL||11-17-2000||01:56 PM||||Fiero's don't have an EGR light, but there is a "Check Engine Soon" light. Your problem may not be related to the egr valve at all. You need to check the error codes or have it done at a shop to find out.<BR>Also you need to give engine size, type, year, etc., for any accurate opinions.<BR>Good luck!||||reg||5
Z||000002||GT-maniac||11-17-2000||02:03 PM||||I meant the check engine light comes on. Since reading the codes always indicates an EGR problem each time I test it I simply called it an EGR light. The car is an 85 GT with the stock 2.8||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||11-17-2000||02:29 PM||||My light come on intermittantly, code 32.  I'm relating it to a vacuum line leak, cause the light will come on while putting some load on the engine (going up a hill) at highway speed.  If I stop the car, shut the engine off, the light doesn't come back on until maybe another load.  It was doing this all this year.  The car never ran better, great gas milage. I installed a new distributor, ignition module this spring and replaced the egr valve two years ago. I have a new egr pipe and selinoid, plus I'm changing rubber vacuum lines.  I do a little bit at a time to see if the problems goes away for good.<P>If your car is running good, I wouldn't worry about it.  ||||reg||11
Z||000004||kornholio||11-17-2000||04:13 PM||||I had that problem when I bought my car last year.  I changed the EGR solenoid (cost me $130 CDN!) and the problem has not returned.||||reg||1
Z||000005||88formula||11-17-2000||04:59 PM||||Running your car without EGR will in the long run harm your engine because you will have detonation even if you can't hear it all the time. Detonation breaks pistons.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Greg Piet||11-18-2000||03:32 PM||||When I had that problem it was teh EGR solenoid not the egr valve...<P>entire solenoid piece, $2.00 at a local boneyard off of a camaro||||reg||1
